{"v":2,"s":"m","w":10,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Angles and triangles","b":"<p>Angles in a triangle add up to <b>180°</b>, in a quadrilateral to <b>360°</b>. Supplementary angles add to 180°.</p><p><b>Pythagoras’ theorem</b> (Pitagorina teorema), for a right triangle with legs a, b and hypotenuse c:</p><div class=\"fx\">c² = a² + b²</div><div class=\"callout\">A ladder against a wall: the ladder is the hypotenuse, the wall and the floor are the legs.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A right triangle: c² = a² + b², so 3² + 4² = 9 + 16 = 25 = 5².\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M60 130 L220 130 L60 30 Z\" class=\"kc a2\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"118\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" class=\"km\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"148\" >b = 4</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"end\">a = 3</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"72\" font-weight=\"700\">c = 5</text></svg><figcaption>A right triangle: c² = a² + b², so 3² + 4² = 9 + 16 = 25 = 5².</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"read","h":"Areas","b":"<table class=\"mini\"><tr><td>Rectangle</td><td>P = a · b</td></tr><tr><td>Triangle</td><td>P = a · h / 2</td></tr><tr><td>Trapezoid</td><td>P = (a + b) · h / 2</td></tr><tr><td>Circle</td><td>P = r²π, perimeter O = 2rπ</td></tr></table>"},{"t":"read","h":"Volumes","b":"<table class=\"mini\"><tr><td>Prism, cube</td><td>V = B · H (cube a³)</td></tr><tr><td>Cylinder</td><td>V = r²πH</td></tr><tr><td>Pyramid</td><td>V = B · H / 3</td></tr><tr><td>Cone</td><td>V = r²πH / 3</td></tr><tr><td>Sphere</td><td>V = 4r³π / 3, surface 4r²π</td></tr></table><div class=\"callout geo\">Geology link: from a sample’s volume and mass you get its density — one way to identify minerals.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three solids you’ll meet in geology labs: a drill core is a cylinder, a volcano is roughly a cone.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"30\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"10\" class=\"kc\"/><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"110\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"10\" class=\"kc\"/><line x1=\"26\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"26\" y2=\"110\" class=\"kc\" /><line x1=\"94\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"94\" y2=\"110\" class=\"kc\" /><text x=\"60\" y=\"140\" >cylinder: r²πH</text><ellipse cx=\"160\" cy=\"110\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"10\" class=\"kc\"/><line x1=\"126\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"22\" class=\"kc\" /><line x1=\"194\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"22\" class=\"kc\" /><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"22\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"110\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"160\" y=\"140\" >cone: r²πH / 3</text><circle cx=\"262\" cy=\"66\" r=\"40\" class=\"kc\"/><ellipse cx=\"262\" cy=\"66\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"11\" class=\"km\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"140\" >sphere: 4r³π / 3</text></svg><figcaption>Three solids you’ll meet in geology labs: a drill core is a cylinder, a volcano is roughly a cone.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"ex","q":"A right triangle has legs 5 and 12. Find the hypotenuse and the area.","s":["c² = 25 + 144 = 169 → c = 13.","Area = 5 · 12 / 2 = 30."],"a":"c = 13, P = 30"},{"t":"num","q":"Two angles of a triangle are 50° and 60°. The third?","a":70,"u":"°","e":"180 − 110."},{"t":"num","q":"Hypotenuse with legs 9 and 12?","a":15,"u":"","e":"√(81 + 144) = √225."},{"t":"num","q":"Area of a circle with r = 10 (π ≈ 3.14)?","a":314,"u":"","e":"100 · 3.14.","tol":0.5},{"t":"num","q":"Volume of a cube with edge 5?","a":125,"u":"","e":"5³."},{"t":"mc","q":"A cone has what fraction of the volume of a cylinder with the same base and height?","o":["1/2","1/3","2/3","1/4"],"a":1,"e":"Three cones of water fill the cylinder."}]}